---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../../components/Hero.astro';
import LangSwitch from '../../../components/LangSwitch.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Privacy policy of the Dragon Gems Swipe app | Ludiven Studio"
	description="Privacy policy of the Dragon Gems Swipe mobile app: no account needed, optional Google or Apple account, public leaderboards, optional video ads, in-app purchases, account deletion, GDPR rights."
	lang="en"
	alternates={{ fr: '/dragons-gems/confidentialite/', en: '/en/dragons-gems/confidentialite/' }}
>
	<div class="wrapper stack gap-12 legal">
		<div class="stack gap-8">
			<LangSwitch lang="en" href="/dragons-gems/confidentialite/" />
			<Hero
				title="Privacy — Dragon Gems Swipe"
				tagline="Only your name and your score are public. Video ads only when you choose them."
			/>
		</div>

		<p class="updated">
			This policy covers <strong>the Dragon Gems Swipe mobile app</strong>
			(<code>com.ludivenstudio.dragonsgems</code>) and its leaderboards, shared with the game on the website
			(<a href="/jeux/eclats/">ludiven-studio.fr/jeux/eclats</a>). The rest of the website has its
			<a href="/confidentialite/">own policy</a> (in French). Last updated: October 31, 2026.
		</p>
		<p class="updated">
			This is a courtesy translation. In case of discrepancy, the
			<a href="/dragons-gems/confidentialite/" hreflang="fr">original French version</a> prevails.
		</p>

		<div class="summary">
			<p><strong>In short:</strong></p>
			<ul>
				<li>The game is played <strong>without an account</strong>. Your progress is kept on your phone.</li>
				<li>An optional <strong>Google or Apple account</strong> saves your progress online, to find it on all your devices.</li>
				<li>The daily challenge, endless mode and summit challenge leaderboards show <strong>your name and your score</strong> to everyone. Nothing else.</li>
				<li><strong>Optional video ads</strong> (Unity) give hearts and coins. They are tailored to your interests only if you agree. No usage analytics. The app asks for neither your location, nor your contacts, nor your photos.</li>
				<li>Optional <strong>in-app purchases</strong> (coins, unlimited hearts), paid through Google Play or the App Store.</li>
				<li>You can <strong>delete your account</strong> at any time from the app's Settings.</li>
			</ul>
		</div>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
			<p>Publisher of the app and data controller:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Company: <strong>Ludiven Studio</strong></li>
				<li>Legal form: EURL (French single-member limited company) with a capital of €1,000</li>
				<li>Registration: 999&nbsp;253&nbsp;586 R.C.S. Vienne — SIRET 999&nbsp;253&nbsp;586&nbsp;00013</li>
				<li>Registered office: 1166 route de la Ranche, 38440 Châtonnay, France</li>
				<li>Contact: <a href="mailto:contact@ludiven-studio.fr">contact@ludiven-studio.fr</a></li>
			</ul>
			<p>See also the <a href="/mentions-legales/">legal notice</a> (in French).</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>2. Without an account</h2>
			<p>
				Your levels, your stars, Bijou's treasure, your hearts, your daily gift and your settings are stored
				<strong>on your phone</strong>. Levels play without a connection.
			</p>
			<p>
				When you finish a daily challenge, an endless game or the summit challenge, the app sends your result
				to the world leaderboard:
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li>your <strong>name</strong>: "Dragon" followed by four digits until you pick one in Settings ("Your name on the rankings"), 20 characters at most;</li>
				<li>your <strong>score</strong> (for the daily challenge, your moves then your time; for endless mode and the summit challenge, your points) and how long the game lasted;</li>
				<li>for the daily challenge, <strong>its date</strong>;</li>
				<li>a <strong>technical id</strong>, drawn at random when the app is installed. It counts your daily try and ties your scores together. It is never shown, never linked to your account, and it changes if you reinstall the app;</li>
				<li>a <strong>submission number</strong>, drawn at random for each game. If the server's answer gets lost, the app sends the same result again, and this number keeps it from being counted twice. The server keeps this number with its answer.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>Without a network, the result waits on your phone and goes out when the connection comes back.</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>3. Your account (optional)</h2>
			<p>
				To save your progress online, you sign in with <strong>Google</strong> or <strong>Apple</strong>, from
				Settings or when the game offers it after level 10. We then receive an account id and your email
				address; with Apple, it may be the relay address that hides yours, or none. We never receive your
				password. With Google, the sign-in service also keeps the name and picture of your Google profile: we
				neither show nor use them.
			</p>
			<p>
				This account is the <strong>Ludiven Studio account</strong>: the same one is used by the Pétanque Meet
				app and the website.
			</p>
			<p>
				Once you are signed in, your progress is copied online: your stars on each level, Bijou's treasure,
				the number of games played, your best endless and summit challenge scores, the star chests opened,
				your daily gift (day and streak), the day of your last daily challenge, your unlimited hearts if you
				bought them, and the treasures of Bijou's and Perle's caves. Your hearts and your settings stay on the
				phone. Your email address is shown only to you, in Settings.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>4. What is public</h2>
			<p>
				Anyone can see the leaderboards, in the app and on the website. They show <strong>your name, your
				score and its date</strong>. Never your technical id, your account or your email address.
			</p>
			<p>
				Your name doesn't have to be your real name: don't put a surname, a number or an address in it.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>5. Data processed</h2>
			<div class="table-scroll">
				<table>
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th>Data</th>
							<th>Purpose</th>
							<th>Legal basis</th>
							<th>Recipient</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr>
							<td>Name, score, game length, challenge date, technical id, submission number</td>
							<td>The daily challenge, endless mode and summit challenge leaderboards; one daily try</td>
							<td>Legitimate interest (GDPR art. 6.1.f) in offering leaderboards</td>
							<td>Supabase; name and score public</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Account id and email address (if you sign in)</td>
							<td>Sign you in, tie your save to you</td>
							<td>Performance of a contract (art. 6.1.b)</td>
							<td>Supabase; Google or Apple for the sign-in</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Google profile name and picture (if you sign in with Google)</td>
							<td>None: kept by the sign-in service, never used</td>
							<td>Performance of a contract</td>
							<td>Supabase</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Save (if you sign in): stars, treasure, games played, best endless and summit challenge scores, star chests opened, daily gift (day and streak), day of the last daily challenge, unlimited hearts bought, treasures of Bijou's and Perle's caves</td>
							<td>Find your progress on all your devices</td>
							<td>Performance of a contract</td>
							<td>Supabase</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Advertising id (on iPhone, only if you allow tracking), other device and app ids, IP address (approximate location), ad interactions, time of use, purchase history, technical information (model, language, screen, connection, performance) and, on Android, the app stores installed</td>
							<td>Show the videos you ask for, measure them, fight fraud; tailor them to your interests if you agree</td>
							<td>Your consent (art. 6.1.a) for tailored ads; legitimate interest (art. 6.1.f) otherwise</td>
							<td>Unity (LevelPlay, Unity Ads, ironSource Ads), which shares them with advertisers</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Your choice about ads</td>
							<td>Remember it and pass it on to Unity</td>
							<td>Legal obligation</td>
							<td>Your phone; Unity</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Product bought, store receipt, transaction number</td>
							<td>Sell, credit and restore your purchases</td>
							<td>Performance of a contract</td>
							<td>Google Play or App Store; Unity (purchase module)</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>IP address</td>
							<td>Carry the exchanges</td>
							<td>Legitimate interest</td>
							<td>Supabase; Unity; Google or Apple during a sign-in</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2" id="publicite">
			<h2>6. Ads</h2>
			<p>
				The game is free. Video ads from <strong>Unity Ads</strong> and <strong>ironSource Ads</strong>, two
				Unity networks, through the <strong>Unity LevelPlay</strong> mediation, are offered to you, always by
				your choice: a heart when you have none left, continuing a lost level, doubling your daily gift, coins
				in the shop, a few times a day. Never during the daily challenge, endless mode or the summit
				challenge.
			</p>
			<p>
				To show these videos, measure them and fight fraud, Unity's module receives your phone's advertising
				id (on iPhone, only if you allow tracking) and other device and app ids, your IP address (which gives
				an approximate location), your interactions with the ads, your time of use, your purchase history,
				technical information (model, language, screen size, connection type, performance) and, on Android,
				the app stores installed on your phone (Google Play, Samsung, Huawei…). We pass on neither your
				account, nor your name, nor your progress.
			</p>
			<p>
				<strong>Your consent.</strong> Before the first video, the game asks whether videos may be tailored to
				your interests ("Yes, tailored" or "No thanks"). Unity's module starts only once you have answered;
				without your consent, the videos are not personalized. For Unity, "No thanks" also opts you out of the
				sale of your data under US state laws. You can change your mind at any time: Settings › "Ad choices".
				On iPhone, after a yes, Apple asks for your permission to track; without it, the iPhone's advertising
				id is not used. You can also reset or delete the advertising id in your phone's settings. To learn
				more: <a href="https://unity.com/legal/game-player-and-app-user-privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Unity's privacy policy</a>.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>7. In-app purchases</h2>
			<p>
				The shop sells coin packs and "Unlimited hearts" (a one-time purchase). Payment is handled entirely by
				Google Play or the App Store: we never see your payment method or your billing address. Unity's
				purchase module receives the proof of purchase from the store; the game credits your purchase and
				keeps its transaction number on your phone. According to Unity, this module may also send it your
				purchase history and technical information about the device.
			</p>
			<p>
				A purchase needs no account; signed in, your unlimited hearts follow your account. "Restore purchases",
				in the shop, gives them back after a reinstall.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>8. What the app does not do</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>No usage analytics</strong> and no crash reports of our own.</li>
				<li>No precise location, contacts, photos or files: the app asks for none of these permissions.</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>9. What is stored on your phone</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>your progress: levels, stars, treasure, hearts, daily challenge played, daily gift;</li>
				<li>your sign-in session and your email address, if you are signed in;</li>
				<li>your name and the leaderboards' technical id;</li>
				<li>your settings: language, theme and reminders;</li>
				<li>your choice about ads, the number of videos watched that day, the numbers of your latest purchases and the results waiting to be sent to the leaderboards; Unity's modules also keep their own data there.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				All of this stays on the device and is erased when you uninstall the app.
			</p>
			<p>
				If you accept them, the <strong>reminders</strong> (the gift of the day, Bijou's full hearts) are
				notifications scheduled by the phone itself: nothing is sent to us for them. You can turn them off in
				the app's Settings or in the phone's.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>10. Recipients, transfers and retention</h2>
			<p>
				We do not sell your data. It is processed only by:
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Supabase</strong> — database, accounts and saves. Data hosted in the European Union (Ireland).</li>
				<li><strong>Unity Technologies</strong> (and its subsidiary ironSource) — video ads (LevelPlay, Unity Ads) and purchase module. For ads, Unity also acts on its own behalf and shares data with advertisers (see <a href="#publicite">Ads</a>).</li>
				<li><strong>Google</strong> and <strong>Apple</strong> — signing in to your account, distributing the app and paying for purchases.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Supabase and Unity are American companies. This transfer is covered by the mechanisms of chapter V of
				the GDPR (standard contractual clauses).
			</p>
			<p>Retention:</p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Account and save</strong>: until you delete your account.</li>
				<li><strong>Leaderboard scores</strong> and their submission numbers: as long as the leaderboard is online. On request, we remove your name and your scores (see §12).</li>
				<li><strong>IP address</strong>: only in Supabase's technical logs, which it erases within a few days.</li>
				<li><strong>Advertising data</strong>: at Unity, under its policy.</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2" id="suppression">
			<h2>11. Delete your account</h2>
			<p>
				In the app: <strong>Settings → "Delete my account"</strong> (the button shows once you are signed in).
				It is immediate and final:
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li>your Ludiven Studio account and your email address are erased;</li>
				<li>your online save is erased;</li>
				<li>since this account is also used by Pétanque Meet, what it holds there is erased or anonymized the same way (see the <a href="/petanque-meet/confidentialite/">Pétanque Meet policy</a>, in French).</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				The progress stored on your phone stays; uninstalling the app erases it.
			</p>
			<p>
				Your leaderboard scores are not tied to your account: they stay under your name. To have them
				removed, write to us with your name.
			</p>
			<p>
				Your unlimited hearts stay tied to your Google Play or Apple account: "Restore purchases" gives them
				back. Advertising data is held by Unity: ask Unity to erase it (<a href="#publicite">link above</a>) or
				write to us and we will pass it on.
			</p>
			<p>
				You can also ask for your account to be deleted by email at
				<a href="mailto:contact@ludiven-studio.fr">contact@ludiven-studio.fr</a>, from your account's address.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>12. Your rights</h2>
			<p>
				Under the GDPR, you have the right of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and
				portability. To use them, or to have a name removed from a leaderboard, write to
				<a href="mailto:contact@ludiven-studio.fr">contact@ludiven-studio.fr</a>. We answer within one month.
			</p>
			<p>
				If you believe your rights are not respected, you can lodge a complaint with the CNIL, the French data
				protection authority (<a href="https://www.cnil.fr" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.cnil.fr</a>),
				3 place de Fontenoy, TSA 80715, 75334 Paris Cedex 07, France, or with your own country's authority.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>13. Children</h2>
			<p>
				The game is not meant for children under 13 and is played without an account. If you are under 15,
				ask your parents before answering "Yes, tailored" to videos, before a purchase and before signing in
				with an account. Pick a name that is not your real name. If you are a parent and want an account or a
				name removed, write to us: we will delete it.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>14. Security</h2>
			<p>
				All exchanges are encrypted (HTTPS). Saves can only be reached through our server: no direct access
				to the database is open. The leaderboards' technical id is never published. Your session is kept in
				the app's storage on your phone.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>15. Changes</h2>
			<p>
				We will update this page with every change of the app that touches your data, with its date at the
				top.
			</p>
		</section>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.legal {
		max-width: 68ch;
		margin-inline: auto;
		color: var(--gray-200);
		font-size: var(--text-md);
		line-height: 1.6;
	}
	.legal h2 {
		font-size: var(--text-xl);
		color: var(--gray-0);
	}
	.legal ul {
		padding-left: 1.2rem;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.35rem;
	}
	.legal a {
		color: var(--accent-regular);
		text-decoration: 1px solid underline transparent;
		text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
		transition: text-decoration-color var(--theme-transition);
	}
	.legal a:hover,
	.legal a:focus {
		text-decoration-color: currentColor;
	}
	.updated {
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
		color: var(--gray-300);
	}
	.summary {
		border: 1px solid var(--gray-800);
		border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-regular);
		border-radius: 0.5rem;
		padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
		background: var(--gray-999_40);
	}
	.summary p {
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}
	code {
		font-size: 0.9em;
		background: var(--gray-999_40);
		padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
		border-radius: 0.25em;
	}
	/* The 4-column table can't shrink below ~40em — scroll it instead of overflowing the page. */
	.table-scroll {
		overflow-x: auto;
	}
	table {
		border-collapse: collapse;
		width: 100%;
		min-width: 36rem;
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
	}
	th,
	td {
		border: 1px solid var(--gray-800);
		padding: 0.5rem 0.65rem;
		text-align: left;
		vertical-align: top;
	}
	th {
		color: var(--gray-0);
	}
</style>
